# Job Hunt Workspace

Generated by the `job-hunt-toolkit:init-workspace` skill. Regenerate by re-running the skill — do not edit by hand, or your changes will be overwritten on the next init.

## Layout

```
./
├── {{FIRST}}_{{LAST}}_{{ROLE}}_CV.typ    # master source (edit this)
├── {{FIRST}}_{{LAST}}_{{ROLE}}_CV.pdf    # master export (regenerate from Typst)
├── README.md
├── AGENTS.md
├── NAMING.md
├── .gitignore
└── jobs/                                  # all applications live here
    └── <company>/                         # one folder per application
        ├── company.md
        ├── job_description.md             # or .<ext> with original extension when user supplies a file
        ├── {{FIRST}}_{{LAST}}_<Role>_CV.typ
        └── {{FIRST}}_{{LAST}}_<Role>_CV.pdf
```

## Workflow

1. Run the `job-hunt-toolkit:new-application` skill with `<company-slug>` — start a new application
2. Run the `job-hunt-toolkit:export-pdf` skill — regenerate any PDF from its Typst source
3. Run the `job-hunt-toolkit:prepare-to-send` skill — run the pre-send checklist before attaching

## Master CV

`{{FIRST}}_{{LAST}}_{{ROLE}}_CV.typ` is the **canonical source**. All edits happen here. The `.pdf` is a regeneratable export.

Never overwrite the master with a tailored variant. Tailored versions live inside `jobs/<company>/`.

## Rules

See `AGENTS.md` and `NAMING.md`. Both are generated pointers; the authoritative rules live in the plugin's skills and `references/`.
